From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: rga: Mirror along the axis the control names

RGA_SRC_MIRR_MODE_X mirrors the picture left to right, MODE_Y top to
bottom, yet the driver set X for V4L2_CID_VFLIP and Y for HFLIP: each
flip control turned the picture the other way. Measured on an RK3528's
RGA2, an NV12 frame against FFmpeg's hflip and vflip: HFLIP matched vflip
exactly, VFLIP hflip, both together a 180 degree turn. Swap the two, for
the source's mirror mode and for the destination corner chosen with it.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga-hw.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga-hw.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga-hw.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rga/rga-hw.c
@@ -221,10 +221,10 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (ctx->vflip)
+	if (ctx->hflip)
 		src_info.data.mir_mode |= RGA_SRC_MIRR_MODE_X;
 
-	if (ctx->hflip)
+	if (ctx->vflip)
 		src_info.data.mir_mode |= RGA_SRC_MIRR_MODE_Y;
 
 	switch (ctx->rotate) {
@@ -353,9 +353,9 @@
 	dst_x = ctx->out.crop.left;
 	dst_y = ctx->out.crop.top;
 
-	if (ctx->vflip)
-		mir_mode |= RGA_SRC_MIRR_MODE_X;
 	if (ctx->hflip)
+		mir_mode |= RGA_SRC_MIRR_MODE_X;
+	if (ctx->vflip)
 		mir_mode |= RGA_SRC_MIRR_MODE_Y;
 
 	switch (ctx->rotate) {
